# SC4MP chat panel. Packed into sc4mp-dll-ui.dat by tools/make-ui-dat.py; the control ids must match ChatPanel.cpp.
# The frames and most buttons are the game's own images, used by their keys like its dialogs do: the steel frame {46a006b0,144161ee} stretched as an
# edge image, its caption button {46a006b0,144161eb} and its up/down buttons {46a006b0,144161e0}/{46a006b0,144161e2}, with its fonts and text color.
# The title has the whole title band, so long server names fit, and the save status is in the bottom band beside Send.
# The other images are drawn by tools/make-ui-images.py, at the size of the windows that show them. Windows are drawn in the order they're listed.
# Each chat line has a text window in the game's text color (0x7B3E9A70 + row), a grey one for lines that aren't chat (0x7B3E9AB0 + row), and a window for the player's name in each of
# the launcher's name colors (0x7B3E9B00 + row * 0x10 + color), since the pinned gzcom-dll has no way to change a text window's color. The colors must match kNameColors in ChatPanel.cpp.
<LEGACY clsid=GZWinGen iid=IGZWinGen id=0x7B3E9A60 area=(8,64,374,298) fillcolor=(0,0,0) caption=" " winflag_visible=yes winflag_enabled=yes winflag_moveable=yes winflag_sizeable=no winflag_sortable=no winflag_pbuff=no winflag_pbufftrans=yes winflag_pbufferase=yes winflag_pbuffvid=no winflag_alphablend=yes winflag_acceptfocus=no winflag_mousetrans=no winflag_ignoremouse=no userdata=0 moveable=yes sizeable=no defaultkeys=no closevisible=no gobackvisible=no minmaxvisible=no closedisabled=no gobackdisabled=no minmaxdisabled=no titlebar=no fill=no outline=no paint=yes sidebar=no gutters=(4,4) >
